# `zag --last` re-renders the most recent session. This scenario is
# best-effort: it assumes a recent prior session exists in
# ~/.local/share/zag/sessions/. The most reliable way to use it is to
# run `slash_quit.zsm` or any other scenario first, then run this one
# back-to-back so the prior session is the freshest on disk.
#
# We anchor on the welcome banner being absent (resume mode skips it)
# and on the presence of some prior-turn artifact in the grid. The
# `wait_text />/` line is a weak signal that the prompt is ready; if
# zag's prompt glyph changes, update this.

spawn ./zig-out/bin/zag --last
wait_idle 2s
snapshot resumed
send "/quit" <Enter>
wait_exit
